# What gcloud must not upload.
#
# `gcloud builds submit` sends the build context to Cloud Build before anything is
# built. Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore - which is close, but not the
# same question: .gitignore says what should not be *committed*, and the things that
# hurt here are the large ones that happen to be committed. reference_docs is 270MB of
# sample certificates in git; graphify-out is generated output that is also in git.
# Both would go up on every build.
#
# Measured before this file existed: about 1.7GB of context, of which some 2.2GB across
# these paths was build output, installers and documents no image has ever needed.
#
# Mirrors .dockerignore deliberately. The two answer the same question for two different
# tools, and a path in one and not the other is how a build context quietly grows back.

.git
.gitignore

# Dependencies - installed inside the image
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output - rebuilt inside the image
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
coverage
**/coverage

# Desktop app: packaged installers, over a gigabyte of them
apps/desktop/release
apps/desktop/.next-standalone
apps/desktop/resources/wireguard-amd64.msi

# Large committed directories no image needs
apps/web-hta/reference_docs
apps/web-hta/storage
graphify-out

# Infrastructure describes the cluster; it does not run in the image
terraform
infra

# Secrets never travel
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Local tooling
.claude
**/.claude
.vscode
.idea
*.log
